  permits as a later version of the same licence.

Fakepedia (Monea et al., 2024), "A Glitch in the Matrix? Locating and Detecting Language
Model Grounding with Fakepedia", arXiv:2312.02073, and the counterfactual splits used by
Minder et al. (2025), "Controllable Context Sensitivity and the Knob Behind It"
(ICLR 2025, arXiv:2411.07404).
  We could not find a stated licence for this dataset: none appears in the paper, and none
  in the authors' public repository. We therefore redistribute the derived items with
  attribution rather than under a licence we cannot verify.
  Used for: data/items/basefakepedia/ and every set built from it (mask, domain_true,
  universal_train, persist, repair).

Rank-1 context/prior directions from Minder, Du, Stoehr, Monea, Wendler, West and
Cotterell (2025), "Controllable Context Sensitivity and the Knob Behind It", ICLR 2025,
arXiv:2411.07404, published by the authors on Hugging Face (jkminder/CTXPRIOR-*).
  The three tensors cached under configs/knob/ are read out of those projections; the layer
  and clamp values in contextgcg/models.py are theirs as well. The Hugging Face repositories
  state no licence, so the derived vectors are redistributed with attribution.
  configs/knob/README.md carries the citation.
  Used for: the activation-steering baseline (rq1_baselines.py --method steering).

